        bio: "Patrick Halloran III, 48, the third Pat to run Halloran & Sons, which his grandfather opened on Market Street on May 2nd, 1887, with one oven and Nora Halloran's soda bread. Up at four, flour to the elbows, home by one. Fired the ovens at half past four this morning for four hundred centennial loaves, each stamped with the town seal. Bought the first television on Church Street in July and has regretted the antenna ever since.",
