        bio: "The Reverend Theodore Ashby, 52, minister of First Congregational — the oldest congregation in town, gathered in 1853, in the present meetinghouse since 1871. A Maine man, a patient fisherman, and a great friend of Father Garrity, with whom he plays checkers every Tuesday in booth four of the Harbor Light Diner, a block from both their churches. Tomorrow's Centennial sermon is on Psalm 107.",
