        bio: "Walter Kowalski, 67, came from near Kraków in 1908 with the first Polish families to work the cannery, and opened Kowalski's Market on Mill Street in 1915 with his savings and a borrowed scale. In July of 1934 he drew a line through every striker's debt in the credit ledger and wrote “Zapłacone. Wszystko.” — Paid. All of it. Nobody had paid anything. Handed the store to his son Ted in '48, but still makes the kielbasa from his mother's recipe.",
