        bio: "Maria Silva, 52, came from São Miguel in the Azores in 1923 and sewed in her kitchen for ten years before she could afford a window on Market Street. Today she dressed four bridesmaids in pink taffeta for the Novak wedding — Helen's cousin Dorota, Peggy Halloran, the Brennan girl and Maria Castellano — and pressed the bride's gown, which she will tell you she did not otherwise touch, because it was perfect.",
